Phase 6 (window verify, perf/RESULTS.md "Phase 6") took ideas, and no code, from:
  ingine  https://github.com/satellitedown/inkling-2-mini-abliterated-ingine  (Apache-2.0)
  basalt  https://github.com/jesdga95/basalt                                    (MIT)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Phase 6 round 2 (perf/RESULTS.md "Phase 6", "Round 2"):

ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu, the kernels ik_mma_moe and ik_q2k_moe, adapt the kernel layout of ingine's
native/src/kernels/moe/moe.cu (moe_up_kernel, slot_mask) and native/src/kernels/dense/gemv.cu (gemv_mma_kernel):
16-row tiles with the tokens of a window as the 8 mma columns, lane (g, t) feeding rows g and g+8 and token g from its
own loads, a fixed-order reduction of the warps' partial tiles through shared memory, and the ballot over the expert
ids by which the first (token, slot) pair owns an expert. Changes: integer operands (mma.sync m16n8k32 s8) unpacked
from GGUF Q2_K / Q2_0 blocks against Q8_1 activations instead of BF16 from NVFP4 / MXFP8, fp32 block scales applied
after the integer sums, a CUDA-core variant with exact block sums, no programmatic dependent launch, no L2 hints.

